{
 "about": "The topic director (Docs/Design/84 \u00a77.3, \u00a78.5; Phase 5). topics: each topic the director may choose, by its sources (kinds; \"_\" the topic's own), their numbers in the director's formulas (base; traveller, grave, festival, broad: the source's own extra; confidence: a deed's confidence's weight; per: a grudge's divisor; step: each further price move less; hourly: the place's draw for the hour, its salt; jitter: the pair's draw, its salt, times jitter_scale), whether it is news or everyday life (the everyday floor and the scorecard's K1 read them), a weight (tuning), the topic graph (next: the topics a talk may pivot to, with the criteria the step needs, \"\" for none) and its aspects (the tiers a pair digs into: conv.aspect). jitter and hourly: the draws' widths. pair_novelty: the same two on the same topic and thing within so many days, times factor. place_saturation: one thing talked of so many times in a place today, times factor. everyday_floor: when more than news_share_over of a place's last window talks were news, everyday topics get boost. favourite: a speaker's favourite topic gets this (favourites: by trait, \"fact=value|value\" over their talk facts; a mantle's from Phase 9). pair_bonus: added to every topic of two by who they are to each other (pair.band): those close talk more. told_once: a claim or one's own news is told a listener once (the talk ledger's told set). topics_per_talk: how many topics a talk may cover (pivots, returns, changes of subject). The numbers began as today's (Tests/fixtures/talk_topics/topics-today.json, ctest talk_topics) and were tuned against the scorecard (doc 84 \u00a730).",
